        "title": "Venus: Runaway Greenhouse and Cautionary Tale",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Venus is Earth's twin by mass and size but has diverged into a hellscape: 737 K surface, 92-bar CO₂ atmosphere, sulfuric acid clouds, and no magnetic field. The divergence from an Earth-like early state makes Venus the most important reference point for understanding long-term planetary climate evolution."
    },
